N2  - Case Detail: A 22 year female came to the hospital with complaints of gastritis, hiccoughs, nausea and vomiting underwent OGD scopy, which revealed lax LES, large hiatus hernia, esophageal and gastric ulcers with H. pylori testing positive on RUT (HP kit taken) 2 months later patient came with complaints of vomiting, dysphagia, cough associated with whitish mucoid expectoration, giddiness since 2 days, and high grade fever since 1 day. On examination, the patient had pulse of 110bpm, BP of 110/70mmhg, spO2 of 90 percent with room air and RR of 28/min. The chest had bilateral crackles. Patient was suspected aspiration pneumonia given her past history. Patient was shifted to ICU, sputum and urine culture sent, and started on Piperacillin/tazobactam and clindamycin and O2. Initial CBC was 10.5/14500/4.1. Creatinine was 1.0. SGOT/PT 493/283. On detailed examination, patient had bilateral upbeat nystagmus, power was reduced on left side (3/5) than right (5/5), absent gag reflex on left side, palatal palsy, reduced sensations on left upper and lower limb. Suspecting lateral medullary syndrome after neurological consultation, an MRI brain was done- s/o hyperintensity in medulla? demyelination ?infarct. Workup for young stroke sent, Sucrose lysis test, APLA profile- all negative. Aspirin and statins started. Considering family history (mother having SLE), an ANA-IF was sent- weak positive. Patient's tachypnea worsened and O2 requirement increased and was electively intubated. She was stated on pulse steroid - injection MPS 1gm IV suspecting Autoimmune demyelinaton- ?MS ?NMO- area postrema syndrome. Patients CSF sent for oligoclonal bands- negative. Routine analysis showed 5 WBCs, 28.4mg/dl proteins and 104 mg/ dl sugars. Serum MOG antibody negative and anti NMO was positive (AQP4). ANA blot sent- showed positivity for anti SSA Ro 60. Neurology review taken who advised pulse steroid for 5 days and then switch to oral prednisolone 1mg/kg. Patient responded to steroid and was extubated on day 4 of pulse steroid. She was kept on NIV and eventually weaned off ventilator. With Extensive chest physiotherapy and suctioning, the patient was weaned off oxygen and shifted to ward. Sputum culture showed pseudomonas and klebsilla species, injection cefepime 1gm iv BD was given and patient improved, with WBC counts normalized and no secretions. Patients condition improved and she was started on tablet prednisolone 60mg. Patient was discharged on prednisolone 40mg and MMF 500mg BD.
