N2  - The proceedings contain 346 papers. The topics discussed include: long-term lung transplant outcomes using current smoker donor lungs; epigenetic study of COPD-risk lung function trajectories; viral bacterial filters change spirometric values in ultrasonic spirometry; location, location, location: interpretability changes in forearm skin prick testing; does daily pollen count adversely affect FeNO measurements?; targeting peripheral airway dysfunction with small particle bronchodilator in asthma; improved FRC accuracy with updated ExhalyserD MBW software in pediatrics; and quality control procedures in respiratory labs across Australia and New Zealand.
