N2  - BACKGROUND Annona muricata leaves extract is a naturally derived solution that has been used to treat a variety of bacterial diseases, including pneumonia, diarrhea, urinary tract infections, and certain skin infections. Nano-sized Zinc oxide particles exhibit significant antibacterial activity over a wide spectrum of bacterial species. A. muricata contains strong phytochemicals called annonaceous acetogenins. They are a group of polyethers with anti-tumor, anti-parasitic, anti-malarial, insecticidal, and antibacterial properties. AIM To analyze the antimicrobial activity of Zinc oxide nanoparticles using extracts of Annona muricata leaves. MATERIAL AND METHODS Aqueous extract of Annona muricata leaves was prepared and after zinc oxide nanoparticle characterisation, antibacterial activity of Annona muricata mediated Zinc oxide nanoparticles against the strains of Staphylococcus aureus, Streptococcus mutans, Enterococcus faecalis and Candida albicans were studied. Mueller Hinton Agar was utilized for this antimicrobial activity by determining the zone of inhibition. RESULTS Annona muricata mediated zinc oxide nanoparticle leaves extract showed dose dependent inhibition of different strains of bacteria as effective as the commercial antimicrobial agent used.
