N2  - Introduction: Post-obstructive pneumonia is usually the result of proximal airway obstruction with distal infection of the lung parenchyma. Intraluminal mass was the most common cause of the obstruction. The postobstructive pneumonia was contributed to the mortality in the patient with the malignancy endo-bronchial lesion. However, little was known the microbiology. This aim of this study was to describe the microbiology of postobstructive pneumonia in patients with malignancy endo-bronchial lesions who undergone bronchial wash. Materials and Methods: From 2011-01 to 2020-12, there were 748 malignant airway obstruction patients at China Medical University Hospital. of these patients, there were 135 patients(18%) with postobstructive pneumonia. All the patients received bronchoscopic tumor excision and bronchial wash. We retrospectively reviewed and analyzed the pathology of tumor and microbiological culture. Results: The mean age were 62.7± 11.8 years old and 117 patients (86.7%) was male. The most common etiology caused endobronchial obstruction were lung squamous cell carcinoma (n=66, 48.9%), esophagus cancer (n=26, 19.3%) and adenocarcinoma (n=22, 16.3%). The most common symptoms were dyspnea (n=120, 88.9%), fever (n=80, 59.3%) and cough (n=36, 26.7%). The most common underlying disease was COPD (n=50, 37%) and 20 patients (14.8%) need ICU care. 37 The most common tumor location were at left main bronchi (n=37, 27.4%) and trachea (n=25, 18.5%). 87 of these patient (64.4%) had received electrocautery, 30 patients (22.2%) had received stent implant and 16 patients (11.9%) had received both electrocautery and stent implant. Microbes were isolated from 109 of 135 patients (80.7%). Among the bacteriology of positive-culture effusions with obstructive pneumonia, Pseudomonas aeruginosa(n=27), Klebsiella pneumonia(n=20), and Streptococcus spp (n=19) were the most common pathogen. Conclusions: The patients with postobstructive pneumonia had high risk to requiring ICU care. Is was important to eliminate the endobronchial tumor and treat with accurate antibiotics. Otherwise, our study provided the common microbiology to choosing accurate treatment for the patients with postobstructive pneumonia.
