N2  - Introduction: Cleaning and disinfection of patient nebulizers is recommended after each use by the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation. Lower airway infection from inhalation of bacterially contaminated medications has been described. Bacteria can also be recovered from home nebulizers after use by CF patients. However, it is unclear if surviving surface bacteria inside the nebulizer can reach the lower airway (ie, dispersion into the respirable fraction) during subsequent inhaled treatments. Methods: Bacterial recovery from the Pari® LC Plus nebulizer after albuterol aerosolization was performed under three different scenarios: 1) Discarded, previously used nebulizers from anonymous CF patients; 2) Nebulizers inoculated with clinical respiratory isolates from CF patients; 3) Nebulizers inoculated with laboratory strains of Pseudomonas aeruginosa (PA01) lacking genes required for different exopolysaccharide (EPS) production. In each scenario, albuterol was aerosolized by Pari® LC Plus nebulizer for 7 minutes with a Vios® air compressor. Aerosolized particles were collected with a refrigerated Next Generation Impactor (NGI) to determine the number of bacteria recovered in the respirable fraction. For each strain, biofilm formation was measured in plastic wells at room temperature after overnight incubation by staining the biofilm with crystal violet and measuring the A595 reading. Results: We cultured bacteria from the respirable fraction of 40% of used CF patient nebulizers using albuterol as the aerosol therapy. S. aureus strains (5/7) were most frequently dispersed compared with only 1/6 P. aeruginosa clinical strains and no Achromobacter (Table). PAO1 lacking Psl dispersed from the nebulizer while wild-type and PAO1 lacking Pel did not, demonstrating the role of Psl in surface attachment. Conclusions: Diverse CF pathogens can leave the nebulizer surface and enter the respirable fraction during inhaled therapies, confirming that re-exposure with bacteria reaching the lower airway is likely to occur when using contaminated nebulizers for home aerosolized therapy.
