N2  - Objective: To investigate the clinical characteristics and etiology of hypereosinophilia Eosinophilic in childrenin order to improve the understanding of this disease. Methods: We analyzed the clinical data of 88 patients who were hospitalised in children'Hospital of Zhejiang University School of medicine from April 2009 to May 2015 retrospectively. Results: Eighty-eight patients were enrolledclinical manifestations of fever in 19 cases (21.6%), abdominal pain in 15 cases (17.0%), cough and tachypnea 14 cases (15.9%), rash in 13 cases (14.8%), hemafecia in 11 cases (1 2.5%), diarrhea in 6 cases (6.8%);etiological factor include infection in 28 cases (31.8%), 11 cases of acute bronchial pneumonia, parasite infection in 9 cases, 4 cases of septicemia, urinary system infection in 2 cases, 1 cases of cellulitis, cholecystitis complicated with pancreatitis in 1 case; allergic disease 25 cases (28.4%); eosinophilic gastroenteritis in 20 cases (22.7%); immunodeficiency disease 3 cases (3.4%), ABO hemolysis, blood system tumors in 2 cases (2.3%). Addicted to eosinophilic cystitis, eosinophilic granulomatous vasculitis, nephrotic syndrome in 1 case respectively; 5 cases with unknown causes (5%). Conclusion: The hospitalized children with hypereosinophilia have a common clinical symptoms with fever and abdominal pain; Infection, allergic diseases and eosinophilic gastroenterirtis is one of the three most common etiology, parasite is the most common pathogens identified; Children with moderate and severe increased eosinophil, should be pay attention to primary immunodeficiency disease.
