N2  - Pulmonary actinomycosis ii a rare disease that is often misdiagnosed as tuberculosis or lonj cancer. Actinomjcei gratteisitjji is a relatively new recognised Actmomyct! species isolated from various clinical samples. The authors report a case of pulmonary actinomycosis caused by A gra<t'fniti. A computed tomography examination revealed an excavated consolidation in tke middle right lobe of a previously healthy young man who presented with a long history of moderate cough. Cultures of the bronchoalveolar lavage fluid confirmed the diagnosis of pulmonary abscess caused by A graveniljfi. At the three-month follow-up consultation and, after six weeks of high- dose amoxicillin, the pulmonary lesion had completely disappeared.
