N2  - Introduction: Sputum of patients with non-cystic fibrosis bronchiectasis (NCFB) contains large numbers of neutrophils and one important chemoattractant is IL-8. Murray et al. showed that Leicester Cough Questionnaire (LCQ) correlates with disease severity and sputum colour chart (SCC) assessment was associated with bacterial colonization, bronchiectasis severity and FEV1. Aims: We wanted to investigate whether lung function, SCC and LCQ also correlated with cell count and IL-8. We also aimed to compare cell count and IL-8 levels in sputum between different etiologies. Methods: 63 patients (27male/36female, average age 59 years ±18) with diagnosis of NCFB were recruited. Underlying etiologies of NCFB were postinfectious causes, primary ciliary diskinesia (PCD), immunedeficiency and idiopathic. Each patient was evaluated by means of spirometry, exhaled NO and LCQ. Exacerbation rate, symptoms of NCFB, retrospective sputum culture results and SCC score (both category and a modified version of the SCC) from their current sputum was analysed. Sputum was induced with hypertonic saline inhalation, total/differential cell count in sputum was assessed and IL-8 was measured in supernatans by means of ELISA. Results: There was a significant difference in sputum IL-8 concentration between the three SCC groups (ANOVA=0.043) with higher purulence resulting in increasing IL-8 levels. IL-8 in sputum also correlated with the modified SCC score (p=0.008,r=0.57), as estimated by the patient. There was a significant inverse correlation between IL-8 levels and FEV1% (r=-0.6,p=0.004) or FVC% (r=-0.54,p=0.015). SCC also correlated with number of positive sputum cultures (p=0.016,r=0.3) and higher SCC category was associated with higher LCQ scores (ANOVA=0.004). Total cell count was significantly different between the three SCC groups (ANOVA=0.0001), with a large difference between the mucous (M) group versus the mucopurulent (MP) and purulent (P) group (median: M: 760,000/ml, MP: 3,780,000/ml, P: 5,080,000/ml). There was a significant correlation between IL-8 and total cell count (p=0.048,r=0.44). Conclusion: In patients with NCFB, sputum colour and lung function were correlated with IL-8 concentrations in induced sputum. There was also an association between sputum colour and the LCQ, the number of positive sputum cultures and total cell count in sputum. NCFB patients with PCD had more airway inflammation (higher total cell count and IL-8 in sputum) than other causes of NCFB.
